 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 515616,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "You’re packing for a trip, for which you need 3 shirts and 3 skirts. If you have 8 shirts and 5 skirts that would work for the trip, how many different ways are there to pack for the trip?",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>It does not matter in which order you pack the shirts and skirts. They will all be with you on the trip.</p> \n<table class=\"unnumbered\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Choices</td>\n<td>3 shirts from 8 shirts</td>\n<td>3 skirts from 5 skirts</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Formula</td>\n<td>8C3</td>\n<td>5C3</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Then, use the Multiplication Rule of Counting. The Multiplication Rule of Counting says that if there are <i>n</i> ways to accomplish one task and <i>m</i> ways to accomplish a second task, then there are <span data-math=\"n{\\text{ }} \\times {\\text{ }}m\"></span> ways to accomplish both tasks. You can tack on additional tasks by multiplying the number of ways to accomplish those tasks to your previous product.</p>\n<p>The number of ways to have the required hand is <span data-math=\"8{\\text{C}}3{\\text{ }} \\times {\\text{ }}6{\\text{C}}3\"></span>.</p>\n<p>Evaluate each combination separately.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"8C3 = \\frac{{n!}}{{r!\\left( {n - r} \\right)!}} = \\frac{{8!}}{{3!\\left( {8 - 5} \\right)!}} = \\frac{{8!}}{{3!5!}} = \\frac{{8 \\times 7 \\times 6 \\times \\cancel{{5!}}}}{{3 \\times 2 \\times 1 \\times \\cancel{{5!}}}} = \\frac{{336}}{6} = 56\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"5C3 = \\frac{{n!}}{{r!\\left( {n - r} \\right)!}} = \\frac{{5!}}{{3!\\left( {5 - 3} \\right)!}} = \\frac{{5!}}{{3!2!}} = \\frac{{5 \\times 4 \\times \\cancel{{3!}}}}{{\\cancel{{3!}} \\times 2 \\times 1}} = \\frac{{20}}{2} = 10\"></span></p>\n<p>Now you can evaluate <span data-math=\"8{\\text{C}}3{\\text{ }} \\times {\\text{ }}5{\\text{C}}3{\\text{ }} = {\\text{ }}56{\\text{ }} \\times {\\text{ }}10{\\text{ }} = {\\text{ }}560\"></span>.</p>\n<p>There are 560 ways to choose 3 shirts and 3 skirts.</p>"
    },
    {
